{"schemaVersion":1,"buildId":"f23bc85995440832e2b6","key":"healthflux","recordId":"healthflux","kind":"paper","lang":"en","title":"A world model simulates the latent dynamics of human health","canonicalPath":"/papers/healthflux/","fields":{"venue":"medRxiv","year":2026,"yearLabel":null,"status":"preprint","statusNote":null,"title":"A world model simulates the latent dynamics of human health","authors":"Wang, Z., Zhang, O., Wang, J., Jiang, Y., Ma, Z. C., …, Gladyshev, V. N., Wyss-Coray, T., Ying, K.","doi":"10.64898/2026.09.19.26363460","link":"https://doi.org/10.64898/2026.09.19.26363460","description":"HealthFlux is a world model built from 502,166 UK Biobank participants. It treats a person's health as one hidden state that changes between visits and is updated by each new blood test, diagnosis, molecular profile or brain and body MRI. In held-out participants it predicts 1,256 diseases and death over twenty years, and it was tested in four independent US cohorts.","descriptions":[{"sourceField":"finding","text":"HealthFlux is a world model built from 502,166 UK Biobank participants. It treats a person's health as one hidden state that changes between visits and is updated by each new blood test, diagnosis, molecular profile or brain and body MRI. In held-out participants it predicts 1,256 diseases and death over twenty years, and it was tested in four independent US cohorts."}],"abstract":null,"descriptionHeading":null,"descriptionSource":null,"pdfDocument":{"available":true,"sourceURL":"https://doi.org/10.64898/2026.09.19.26363460","openPaperHref":"https://doi.org/10.64898/2026.09.19.26363460","displayPolicy":"all-pages","rightsDecision":false,"identityDecision":false,"version":"preprint","licence":"not stated","pageCount":60,"renderedPages":60,"readingWidth":2048,"loupe":{"mode":"magnify-same-image","factor":2},"manifestHref":"/content/papers/healthflux.json"},"pdfFigures":[{"figureNumber":1,"href":"/assets/papers/healthflux/figure-01.webp","legendFirstSentenc